    "body": "## Ada examples: opt-in highlighting and verified API links\n\nv0.1.4 adds opt-in Ada syntax highlighting in developer-guide examples, with source/native-verified API hyperlinks. Source-verified homepage examples can optionally receive the same static highlighting.\n\nConfigure these three options under `[guides]`:\n\n```toml\n[guides]\nada_example_highlighting = true\nada_example_api_links = true\nada_landing_example_highlighting = true\n```\n\nThe options default to `false`; retain the other required settings in your existing `[guides]` configuration. API linking is conservative: a reference must agree with public Ada source and the native GNATdoc declaration/anchor. Ambiguous overloaded routines, including `Create` and `Clone`, are left unlinked rather than choosing an arbitrary overload. Unsupported or unverified references are also left unlinked.\n\nRendering is static and works offline, without a browser syntax highlighter, CDN, or new runtime dependency. With the features disabled, qualified output remains compatible with v0.1.3 except for version-bound presentation metadata.\n\n## Compatibility and adoption\n\n- Supported qualification contract: Python 3.11\u20133.13 and GNATdoc 26.0.0.\n- Optional guide Markdown dependencies remain pinned to `markdown-it-py==3.0.0` and `mdurl==0.1.2`; the core package has no mandatory runtime dependencies.\n- Consumers must regenerate from pristine GNATdoc output and independently qualify adoption. Package qualification is not consumer migration or production-deployment certification. This release does not claim that Core, Geometry, Imgproc, or MEL already use v0.1.4 in production.\n\n## Qualified release artifacts\n\nThese are the exact four GNATDOC-029 qualified artifacts, without rebuilding or substitution: the wheel, source distribution, `release-provenance.json`, and `SHA256SUMS`.\n\n- Approved merged-main commit: `2200eb0e95e769a70d3d38a6c8b7facce8205924` (merged PR #25).\n- Approved source tree: `a0c1038b8332c3ff040b678d393f2871e7d5eeb4`.\n- Exact-main CI: [run 41228082286](https://github.com/zackboll/ada-gnatdoc-enhancer/actions/runs/41228082286), all eight jobs successful.\n- GNATDOC-029 retains a 6,327-test source/wheel/rebuilt-sdist matrix on Python 3.11\u20133.13, archive/RECORD/source audits, conformance, security, and local browser qualification evidence.\n\nVerify the three payloads with `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`. The unchanged provenance field `publication_authorized = false` records that the qualification artifact cannot independently authorize publication; separate explicit repository-maintainer authorization permits this GitHub release.\n\nNo consumer upgrade, Pages deployment, PyPI publication, or Alire publication is included."
